infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title HTTP/2 over TCP vs HTTP/3 over QUIC
  desc Same multiplexing, different transport — the tradeoff is loss isolation vs CPU and reliable-link speed
  compares
    - label HTTP/2 over TCP
      children
        - label Loss recovery is per connection
          desc One lost packet stalls all streams (TCP HOL blocking)
        - label Separate TCP then TLS handshake
          desc Cold setup adds round-trips before TLS 1.3
        - label Identified by the 4-tuple
          desc IP change resets the connection, new 1–2 RTT handshake
        - label Wins on reliable wired links
          desc Low loss, no userspace QUIC CPU cost — faster datacentre east-west
    - label HTTP/3 over QUIC
      children
        - label Loss recovery is per stream
          desc Only streams in the lost packet retransmit; others keep flowing
        - label TLS 1.3 integrated into the handshake
          desc Cold connection 1 RTT; 0 RTT on resumption
        - label Identified by a connection ID
          desc Survives IP change via connection migration, no re-handshake
        - label Wins on lossy and long-RTT paths
          desc Mobile and intercontinental — at extra userspace CPU cost
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
